  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anticipatory Humanitarian Action for Displacement (AHEAD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Anticipatory Humanitarian Action for Displacement (AHEAD) programme of the Danish Refugee Council (DRC) is focused on a reduction of upward pressure on humanitarian needs due to conflict-induced displacement, through expansion of anticipatory action (AA) approaches, which will enable a more timely, dignified, efficient and sustainable humanitarian response. The DRC will focus on anticipatory action data models and approaches using local and global data for insightful local level analysis to help humanitarian actors&#x2019; decisions in deploying humanitarian assistance.

The programme will focus on:
- ensuring that humanitarian actors can easily access accurate DRC displacement models
- expanding existing DRC AA methods for conflict-induced displacement, fostering inclusive practices for local actors
- building the evidence base: piloting our AA approaches, and commission robust evaluation.
- engaging with policymakers to build a supportive environment for the expansion of AA.</narrative>
  </description>
